\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{Reversion and the pseudoscalar}
\date{2026-11-13}

\p{Reversion is the anti-automorphism #{\tilde A} that fixes #{V_x}
and reverses products. Voight's reversal is this reversion
#{\tilde A}. It is an #{R}-linear involution of the even
Clifford algebra in
\citet{22.2.10, p. 347}{voight2021quaternionv107u}, when
#{R} is a noetherian domain, the module is projective of
finite rank, and the value module is invertible.}

\p{The full Clifford functor under isometries is
\citet{Remark 22.2.13, p. 347}{voight2021quaternionv107u}.
The even Clifford functor in similarities is
\citet{Theorem 22.2.11, p. 347}{voight2021quaternionv107u}.
The two functors are not the same.}

\p{The pseudoscalar is the chosen generator #{\psI} of the top
exterior power.}

\p{Creation and annihilation are #{e_i\wedge} and #{e_i\cdot}.
Exterior-algebra texts write them #{\epsilon_i} and #{\iota_i}, and their sum #{\epsilon_i+\iota_i} is the Clifford generator #{e_i\wedge+e_i\cdot}.}
